---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import StoreBadges from '../components/StoreBadges.astro'
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Bondfires was built by two engineers, David and Jake, whose friendship kept dying in the group chat. Here’s why they built a video app for small groups, and what they believe."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">About Bondfires</p>
      <h1>We built the thing we needed.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Bondfires exists because the people we care about most were the people we talked to least.
        Not for lack of wanting to. For lack of a Tuesday night that worked for everyone.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section founders">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <div class="people">
        <!-- TODO(David, Jake): replace initials with real portraits (square, ≥800px). -->
        <figure>
          <span class="portrait">D</span>
          <figcaption><strong>David Eggertsen</strong><span class="muted">Co-founder</span></figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <span class="portrait alt">J</span>
          <figcaption><strong>Jake</strong><span class="muted">Co-founder</span></figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>

      <div class="prose">
        <h2>The story</h2>
        <p>
          We’re two engineers who have been friends for a long time. Somewhere along the way, careers
          and kids and different cities turned the friendship into a group chat. Hundreds of messages a
          month, and none of them the conversation either of us actually wanted to have.
        </p>
        <p>
          We tried scheduling calls. Calendar tetris, every time. We tried voice notes. Better, but
          they vanish into the same scroll as everything else. What we wanted was simple: a way to say
          the real thing, with our actual faces, and have the other person answer the same way when they
          got a minute.
        </p>
        <p>
          So we built it, first for our own groups. It turns out a lot of groups have the same
          problem. The monthly meeting is the only time anyone says anything that matters, and it’s
          the first thing to get cancelled.
        </p>

        <h2>What we believe</h2>
        <h3>Depth over volume</h3>
        <p>
          Most of the internet is optimised for how much you post. Bondfires is optimised for whether
          the four people who matter actually heard you. Camps are small on purpose. Threads stay
          threads. There is no public feed to perform for.
        </p>
        <h3>Your time is yours</h3>
        <p>
          Nobody should have to be free at eight o’clock to be a good friend. Everything in Bondfires
          works on your schedule: record when you can, watch when you can, reply when you can.
        </p>
        <h3>Your conversations are yours</h3>
        <p>
          Videos are visible only to the camp they were posted in. We don’t sell data, we don’t run
          ads, and we don’t use your conversations to train anything or target anyone. We make money
          the plain way: some members pay for <a href="/pricing">Plus, Premium, or Pro</a>.
        </p>
        <h3>Accessible by default</h3>
        <p>
          Joining a camp, watching, and replying are free and will stay free. Real community
          shouldn’t require a retreat weekend and a four-figure invoice.
        </p>

        <h2>Where we are</h2>
        <p>
          Bondfires is live on iOS and Android and is run by the two of us. The first camps are our
          own groups and the groups of people who asked to try it. If you lead a group and want to be
          one of them, <a href="/for/groups">start here</a>. If you just want to say hello,
          <a href="mailto:support@bondfires.org">support@bondfires.org</a> reaches both of us.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2>Come sit by the fire.</h2>
      <StoreBadges campaign="about" />
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .narrow {
    max-width: 780px;
  }
  h1 {
    max-width: 14ch;
  }
  .founders {
    padding-top: 0;
  }
  .people {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-7);
  }
  figure {
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }
  figcaption {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2px;
  }
  .portrait {
    width: 84px;
    height: 84px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.8rem;
    background: radial-gradient(circle at 30% 30%, var(--charcoal), var(--gunmetal));
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--iron);
  }
  .portrait.alt {
    background: radial-gradient(circle at 30% 30%, var(--ember), var(--gunmetal));
  }
  .cta {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--iron);
  }
  .cta h2 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-5);
  }
</style>
